$ chap git setup
exit: 0
--- git
git config --local --replace-all url.http://127.0.0.1:55398/git/.insteadOf https://github.com/
git config --local --replace-all credential.http://127.0.0.1:55398/git/.helper 
git config --local --add credential.http://127.0.0.1:55398/git/.helper !f() { echo username=chap; echo "password=$CHAP_RUN_TOKEN"; }; f
--- request
(none)
--- stdout
git now sends https://github.com/ traffic to http://127.0.0.1:55398/git/ (local)
push authenticates with CHAP_RUN_TOKEN from the environment; no token is stored
